Section: PART I: INTRODUCTION AND APPLICABILITY > 3. DEFINITIONS
Definition: Virtual Asset Service Providers (VASP)

Virtual Asset Service Providers (VASP)

means any natural or legal person who is not covered elsewhere under the FATF Recommendations, and as a business conducts one or more of the following activities or operations for on behalf of another natural or legal person:
(a)exchange between virtual assets and fiat currencies;
(b)exchange between one or more forms of virtual assets;
(c)transfer of virtual assets;
(d)safekeeping and/or administration of virtual assets or instruments enabling
control over virtual assets; and
(e)participation in and provision of financial services related to an issuer’s offer and/or sale of a virtual asset.

